# matlatl corpus excludes (gitignore syntax). Files matched here are removed
# from the doc graph entirely — not scanned, not link-checked, not ranked.
# Use this for markdown that is NOT documentation. For scaffolding that should
# stay link-checked but hidden from the consumption surfaces, use emitExclude
# in .matlatl.yml instead.

# Transient working notes — plans, phase/review briefs, scratch. Gitignored and
# disconnected by nature; left in, they dominate orphan/compactness metrics.
# (matlatl already auto-ignores .claude/agent-memory, .claude/plans,
# .claude/worktrees; .scratch is the same kind of thing.)
.scratch/

# Root-level review and handoff artifacts are transient working notes, not product documentation.
review-*.md
report*.md
handoff-*.md
handover-*.md

# Claude Code sub-agent definitions (reviewer/specialist agents). These are
# isolated by nature — no inbound or outbound doc links — so there is nothing to
# link-check; keeping them in the corpus only adds orphan findings that block a
# `check --strict` gate. Ignored (not just emitExclude'd) so --strict can pass.
# (Skill definitions in .claude/skills/ DO link to docs, so they stay in the
# corpus via emitExclude in .matlatl.yml — link-checked but hidden from the
# navigation surface.)
.claude/agents/

# End-to-end test fixtures — intentionally standalone markdown (fake souls,
# skill definitions, workspace READMEs) consumed by the e2e harness, not docs.
# e2e/README.md (the suite's own documentation) deliberately stays in the corpus.
e2e/fixtures/

# mecatequi PR-body templates. These are NOT documentation — they are
# {{placeholder}}-token templates rendered by publish.sh into a PR description
# (pr-body.md is the dogfooded live template; pr-body.md.example is the copyable
# sample). They carry no doc links — a token like `[Workflow run]({{run_url}})`
# only LOOKS like a markdown link, and the files are navigationally isolated — so
# leaving them in the corpus only adds a spurious broken-link + orphan that block
# `check --strict`. The operator-facing prose lives in docs/usage.md +
# docs/adr/0028-mecatequi.md, which DO stay in the corpus.
.github/mecatequi/

# GitHub issue and pull-request templates are rendered by GitHub rather than read
# as repository documentation. Their links are convenience references for a
# reporter or contributor, not graph navigation, so scanning them makes their
# intentionally unlinked template roots unreachable under `check --strict`.
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/
.github/pull_request_template.md

# CLAUDE.md is a symlink to AGENTS.md (the canonical contract) for Claude Code
# compatibility. It is not a separate corpus document.
CLAUDE.md

# user-docs/ is the mecatl.dev Docusaurus site content — user-facing docs
# derived from the internal architecture and usage docs. Excluded until the
# content is reviewed and stable; links use Docusaurus content-root-relative
# paths that matlatl doesn't understand anyway (no content-root aliasing).
user-docs/

# website/AGENTS.md is agent guidance for the Docusaurus site, not product docs.
# website/CLAUDE.md is a compatibility symlink to that canonical file.
website/AGENTS.md
website/CLAUDE.md

# API Extractor reports are review artifacts, not navigational documentation.
# Exclude both the committed reports and their ignored comparison copies.
sdk/typescript/etc/*.api.md
sdk/typescript/.api-extractor-temp/
